-- title:
--   Integrality over A[j] descends to all large number fields
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and a natural number $N \neq 0$; write $M = Nq$. Let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M`, that is of the subfield of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions `divisorExpansions M`. Assume $f$ satisfies a monic polynomial equation with coefficients in `affineBaseFin M A`, the subring of `modularFunctionFieldBar M` generated by the constants coming from $A$ (via `constantsHom`) together with the element `jBar M`; in Lean this is the existence of a monic $p$ over that subring with `eval₂` of $f$ along the inclusion equal to $0$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite extension $K'$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $K \le K'$, such that for every finite $K'' \supseteq K'$ the Laurent series underlying $f$ lies in `jIntegralClosure M A K''`, i.e. it lies in `fieldOver M K''` — the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series of elements of $K''$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $M$ — and is integral over `jRing A K''`, the subring generated by the constant series of `coeffSubring A K''` together with `jqModC`.
--
--   This is the descent step for $\mathfrak q$-expansions: a modular function on $X_0(Nq)$ with algebraic Fourier coefficients that is integral over the affine ring $A[j]$ of the $j$-finite chart already lies, cofinally in the number field $K''$, in the integral closure of $(A \cap K'')[j]$ inside $K''(j, j_{Nq})$. It is used in the analysis of prolongation tuples at a place specialisation, where values and residues of such functions must be computed over a single number field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_forall_mem_jIntegralClosure_of_integral_affineBaseFin.lean

